pon that  has one of the best fire rates in the  game so you can ink turf get in and out  and really quickly move around the map  so if you can get in close and fast  against your opponents this is a weapon  that you'll have a hell of a time way  all right next up our blasters and  blasters are kind of the second cousins  to the shooter they're halfway between a  grenade launcher and a shotgun and so  what they'll do is shoot out a small  blob that explodes after a certain  distance and now these are a little bit  harder to use since they are slower and  they don't have the rapid-fire element  like the shooters do but they do have  the advantage of being able to hit  people around corners and so what you  want to do with them is kind of time  your shots maybe throw out a shot make  sure it hits and then back up try get  your second shot to splat them what  blasters are really good at though are  taking out groups of Inklings so anytime  you see people crowded together or if  there's a bunch of people on the tower  or splat zones you want to make sure you  have a blaster on hand to take out a  couple of them at a time now this is  more of a personal preference but I  really like blasters that have a huge  blast radius and a really short range so  I can get up close and splat them  immediately  now the first game had one called the  Luna blaster and it's in this game -  you'll have to wait till level 19 to  unlock it but trust me it's worth it  okay next up our rollers and rollers are  among one of the most unique weapons  you'll ever see in the shooter now their  main purpose is usually for inking as  they lay down the wide path of ink  wherever they walk but they have a lot  of power to them - because you can  remember to roll over anyone in one hit  these so that means you do have to be  close to them so what you want to do is  kind of hide in the ink sometimes and  then jump out and then splat them one  thing that you want to try to avoid  though is chasing people as you can be  kind of a sitting duck if you're trying  to run after someone like that also you  can jump an attack to fling ink in a now  vertical manner as opposed to the  horizontal way in the first mattoon and  what this does it helps you reach walls  to climb up and also help reach faraway  enemies and it also helps with the  rollers main weakness which is forward  momentum normally it was difficult for  rollers to escape since the ink that  they paint was always behind them but  now with the vertical flick you can  actually give a path to move forward  making it you know just as fast as other  weapons when you're trying to get from  one place to another and if you're just  starting out the standard splat roller  loadout is actually really good has the  curling bomb which helps you with your  4-momentum even more  and squash I will really really help you  when you're cornered alright next up  we're gonna be talking about brushes and  brushes are kind of similar to rollers  in that they leave a trail of ink  wherever you walk but they're  interesting for a couple different  reasons one because they grant you some  of the fastest movement speed while  using the weapon in the game like you  can make a path from your spawn to their  spawn in pretty much no time they also  have a very powerful melee attack at  point-blank range there aren't many  weapons that are better it's very  difficult to react to a surprise attack  with a brush and it also gives you a  pretty big spread of ink so if you get  to a high location you can just wipe it  around and spread ink all over the place  now so what you want to do with brushes  is kind of use it to your advantage use  the speed to your advantage  get into their territory early pop up  hit them with a brush run out you know  hit-and-run tactics are very very useful  with brushes but one thing that you want  to watch out for is ink usage because  they use a lot of ink and because of the  fact they leave such a narrow strip it's  going to be hard to find good patches of  ink to recharge your weapon with so if  you go up on the offensive you probably  need to be stealthy you know going up  against something like a shooter or a  slasher will probably cause you some  troubles but if you can sneak in and  splash some ink run away repeat pretty  much good to go alright next up are  chargers and charges are a splatoon's  version of the sniper rifle it's a very  powerful weapon and actually a personal  favorite of mine so shots what the  charger will travel really far compared  to any other weapon in the game and  they'll also lay down a lane of ink  behind it depending on how long you  actually hold the charge for and now  they may seem a little bit slow to use  that you can't really move too much  while actually aiming them but what they  do is they lay down that lane of ink a  really long way and then you can  actually use that Lane to swim so with  the charger you can actually travel  great distances really really quickly  and you want to incorporate your  vertical movement along with that they  only take one shot in order to paint an  entire wall so you can use it to climb  walls and reach high points and so from  up there you can snipe people and also  lay down lanes of ink that will help cut  the enemy off so since you are a sniper  pretty much if an enemy gets close to  you you'll want to immediately run away  you know use your sub weapon whatever  you got just try to create some distance  between you and the other inkling  because nine times out of ten you'll  probably lose in a firefight to a  shooter and also real quick one new  feature that they added for Chargers is  the ability to hold your charge while  swimming in the ink so if you have a  fully charged shot you can actually dive  down to the ink for about a second or  two pop up and let it go  it's good for when you need to  reposition but also it's really good for  sneak attacks and so as far as personal  recommendations go I 